# graph: shortest-path and heuristic-search algorithms in boru.
#
# STATUS — DESIGNED, NOT IMPLEMENTED.
#
# This module is a scaffold. The `Graph` namespace exported at the bottom
# is deliberately EMPTY: no algorithm, no representation, no helper is
# written yet. The argued design — what the family is, how the graph is
# represented, the priority-queue primitive the whole family rests on,
# and the boru constraints that force each shape — lives in DESIGN.md at
# the repository root. Read that before adding anything here.
#
# The planned roster (see DESIGN.md §4) is the shortest-path family:
# Dijkstra, A*, greedy best-first, Bellman-Ford, Floyd-Warshall, and the
# DAG-shortest-path special case — one engine with a pluggable priority.
#
# --- representation ---
#
# Not yet fixed. DESIGN.md §5 records the candidate shapes (weighted
# adjacency Map vs edge list), the String-key constraint boru imposes on
# node names, and the direction ruling inherited from the sibling `sort`
# library's topological-sort design.
#
# Calling convention: forward args, receiver (the graph) LAST —
# `Graph.verb …args g`, with the piping form `g Graph.verb …args end`
# equally valid. This matches every sibling library in the ecosystem and
# is fixed now so the design cannot drift from it later.
#
# Imported via `import "./graph.aql"`; the importing script need not
# pre-import the `boru:*` utilities this module will eventually use.

export "Graph" {
}
